WEBVTT

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:12.550
What now?

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.730
If you're gonna try to take
the Dragon Torque, I'll fight you.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:21.250
Damn. You're completely nuts.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.330
Do you think you can fight me
in the shape you're in?

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:30.510
You have no respect for me,
do you? Take a look.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.350
Can't you tell the wavering
of this dimension is getting worse?

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.790
That's because La'cryma
interfered with this dimension.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:42.890
If this dimension is blown apart,
the Dragon Torque will be lost.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.720
I won't let that happen.
I will protect Haruka.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.260
I will not let you people have her.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.570
Now that you're cut off
from the pipeline...

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.870
you're eventually going to
perish in this place, y'know.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:07.380
Thanks to you...

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:16.550
Well, I suppose we can always secure
the Dragon Torque at our leisure after you're gone.

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:22.980
Guess I'll reschedule our showdown
for our next encounter.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:02:01.010
Karasu!

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:11.640
At the silver sky, the endless sky

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:17.970
I gazed together with you, without a word

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:24.150
Touching your back, with trembling fingers

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:29.580
I quietly ponder, as your profile looks up

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:35.620
I want to assure your smile, and the future ahead of you

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:41.960
Just standing and crying, I want to erase myself away

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:47.840
As I extend my hands, it is almost within my reach

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:53.890
This is no fantasy, possibilities are perhaps right by my side

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:59.730
Changing every sorrow into strength

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:05.900
Let's throw all limitations into the end of time

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:09.090
Just keeping you as my aspirations

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:14.240
Even in the driving wind

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:21.180
I'll still be pushing on ahead

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:26.840
Misekku kesta

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:34.760
Fortune. Will you save it for me, dear?

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.120
Hey, wait!

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:10.260
Why the forced re-direction?!

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:13.190
An unforeseen situation came up.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.270
Fukuro, you...

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:22.280
Shinohara, huh? The president
of a telecommunications company...

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.010
sure acts big for his britches.

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:27.580
It can't be helped. One third of
the funds for the Magic Circle Project...

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:31.250
is being invested by his company.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:35.590
But your Ab-Com is supposed
to be supervising that, right?

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:38.030
We're a nuisance to him.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:41.460
He just wants to halt the preliminary
investigation and give the okay.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.330
All he wants to do is to perform the
actual test on quantum teleportation.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:46.230
Quantum teleportation?

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.410
If you make an alteration to a single
simultaneously generated quantum...

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:54.010
the same alteration will occur
to the other quanta.

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:56.600
That is called quantum teleportation.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.550
It's a system that uses
the properties of quanta...

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:02.850
to instantaneously send
large quantities of information.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:06.450
That is the Magic Circle Project the
government is working on right now.

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:12.530
Among the quanta, we directed
our attention to the theta particles.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:14.960
This is probably the
smallest unit of matter.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:19.790
The government is considering
applying this to the quantum teleportation.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.400
If this is completed,
they say it will change the world...

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.430
far greater than the industrial revolution.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.640
Quanta, huh? Is it dangerous?

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:33.640
Theta particles influence
the place-site of quantum potential.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.640
Quantum potential?

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.770
To put it simply,
dimensions are twisted.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:41.420
Dimensions?

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.360
I have a feeling that
all of the unexplained events...

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:47.360
are the result of contact
with other dimensions.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:51.460
Other dimensions? Explain it to me
in a way I can actually understand.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:56.010
Other dimensions, as in the
mulitverse interpretation of quantum theory.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:59.670
The mulitverse interpretation
of quantum theory? What's that?

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.680
God doesn't roll the dice.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:05.270
Dice?

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:07.980
It's a metaphor for people like you...

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:10.450
who don't believe in
the uncertainty of a quantum world.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.850
The uncertainty of a quantum world?

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:18.430
Let's say you roll the dice
and it comes up a 6.

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:20.920
I prefer 1s myself. They're red.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.520
All right, a 1 it will be.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:29.600
Let's say you rolled a 1. But you
could have also rolled a 5 or a 4, right?

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:31.270
All the odds are the same.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:32.440
Well, yeah.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:36.120
And what if there was a world where you
rolled a 5 and a world where you rolled a 4?

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:37.580
Uh?

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.650
Say there are countless worlds...

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:44.580
where your countless self
is rolling countless amount of dice.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:48.720
Now hold on there, Uchida-chan. Do you
seriously believe in that sort of thing?

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:52.460
This is the way they think
in quantum physics:

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:55.530
The tiniest elementary quanta
that compose matter...

00:06:55.530 --> 00:07:00.100
are just too small to be
observed in their natural state.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:04.340
So the microscope to observe something
that small hasn't been invented?

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:06.640
No, there's more to it.

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:10.450
For a human to observe an object,
we must hit it with light...

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.750
and look at its reflection.

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:17.450
But quanta are almost the same size
as the photons that create light...

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:22.290
so just hitting them with light has a large
effect on the quanta we are observing.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:27.460
That makes sense. So now I know
that you can't properly observe quanta...

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:31.840
but what does that have to do with
the existence of several worlds?

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:35.170
Not being able to observe them...

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:38.770
means that we can't tell what state
the quanta are in at any given time.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:42.270
In other words,
infinite possibilities will exist.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:44.690
What does that mean?

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:51.290
For example, if you logically consider
where a single quantum might exist...

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:55.420
there is the possibility of it existing
in various places until it is observed.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:57.990
Just because you can't see something...

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:00.620
I doubt that means it's everywhere...

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.300
Uh-uh. Not just exist...

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:07.100
but the possibilities
of existence are infinite.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:09.290
Possibilities...

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:14.110
Yes. And all matter in the world...

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:16.040
naturally, including you and I...

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:18.520
are made from accumulations
of those small quanta.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:19.810
Hold on a second.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:24.550
You said the location of the existence
of quanta is not definite...

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:26.750
but I'm right here...

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:30.020
And this table and that glass
are all right here, correct?

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:35.070
That's where quantum physics
becomes difficult to explain.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:40.400
Even if existence is steadfast
on an everyday macro level...

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.680
the moment it's taken
to the quantum micro level...

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.640
its existence becomes ambiguous.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.570
I think I'm getting a headache.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:52.170
This entire world consists
of such unstable little quanta.

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:58.350
And if so, it's possible to believe
that this entire universe...

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.860
is branching off moment by moment...

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:03.850
into infinite universes
with unlimited possibilities.

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:08.860
Is that what you meant when
you just said that worlds exist...

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:11.160
where I don't roll a 1?

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:24.620
It's "the multiverse interpretation" theory
in what is called quantum mechanics.

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:30.420
Countless worlds are lined up in
an endless row, like opposing mirrors...

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:33.350
where countless selves
are rolling countless dice.

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:39.090
Do you seriously believe in
alternate worlds, Uchida-chan?

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:43.220
We call them
alternate dimensions, but yes.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:48.480
In a quantum world, there is one other
coordinate that transcends time and space.

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:51.170
The equation that
indicates that coordinate...

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:53.710
is testimony to the existence
of alternate dimensions.

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:56.360
Although its existence
is strictly numerical.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:01.580
Is it possible to go to
those alternate worlds?

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:05.110
It might be possible if we were
to become a quantum existence.

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:07.860
Becoming an uncertain existence...

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:11.550
to travel to an uncertain alternate
dimension may be theoretically possible.

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:15.130
I feel like I'm having a bad hangover.

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:21.170
A long time ago, people who thought
that the sun revolved around the earth...

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:24.940
had a hard time believing that
it was the opposite, right?

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:29.840
It takes time for people to discard
what they have always believed...

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:31.610
to be common sense.

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:34.210
Alternate dimensions.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:38.520
If it's as you imagine,
what will happen after this?

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:43.520
The stability of the quantum
dimensions will be lost...

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:45.960
and every dimension will expire.

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:48.460
The entire cosmos will be wiped out.

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:59.680
Your mom said you don't have to study
anymore if you don't want to, right?

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.510
Something like that...

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:03.950
Okay, then come back
to the soccer team.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:08.520
I told you already.
I don't have your soccer sense.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.820
It's not like you have
to go pro or nothing.

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:13.450
Just do it for your health.

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:16.680
I'm not an old man, so that's no reason.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:18.750
Really?

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:21.740
So it isn't good enough
to just like the game?

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.590
I'll pass on it.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:27.490
Then what do you want to do?!

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.830
I'm having trouble figuring that out.

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:37.610
I've been thinking about
what I want to do with my life.

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:39.010
And?

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:43.990
I do like soccer,
but not as much as you do...

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:45.820
and besides, I'm not very good at it.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:47.850
If you wanna get good at it, then practice!

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:49.720
I did, remember?

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:52.990
I practiced right beside you
since third grade.

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:54.350
Well, yeah, but...

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:57.110
I don't have the talent for it.

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.700
Sports, art, and music...

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:04.870
are for the ones who
are born with the talent.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.200
That's not true!

00:12:06.770 --> 00:12:10.200
So I understood what my mom said.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:14.040
The more you study,
the more your grades go up.

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:16.800
Even a no-talent wonder
like me can do that.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.620
But I can't study whatsoever.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:22.050
That's because you never try.

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:25.690
All you need to do is give up
some of your play time.

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:27.220
That's why...

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.310
Yeah?

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:31.570
I think I should take the exams.

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:35.070
How come?! If you
go to school in Tokyo...

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:37.070
you won't be able
to see the gang anymore!

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:39.270
I don't like that either, but...

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:42.570
Then give up on the exams.
Chuck 'em!

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:45.280
You're such a child, Isami.

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:48.610
You can't have everything your way.

00:12:48.610 --> 00:12:51.250
You can do anything
if you have the power to believe!

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:53.960
That's what I mean by childish
to think like that.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.860
Shut up, shut up!

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:58.290
Argh, I'm getting ticked off!

00:12:58.290 --> 00:12:59.950
You're such an idiot!

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:04.330
You're impossible!

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:18.110
Karasu, Fukuro...

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:22.110
Stop that, Atori.
Irritation will wear you out.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:24.280
I'll kill 'em!

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:11.580
Hmm, seems pretty bad.

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:25.840
Guess I'll make lunch.

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:32.680
Too much trouble!

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:40.770
It's lunch time!

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:42.000
What?

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:45.190
You're kidding!
You actually made lunch, Mom?!

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:49.350
Is this it?

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:50.250
That's it.

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:52.210
Well, dig in!

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:53.730
Okay...

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:57.080
Thank you for this bounty.

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:04.290
Yummy?

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:05.460
Uh-huh.

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:07.520
Any closer to solving your problem?

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:08.260
Huh?

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:12.010
With more experience in life,
I would be happy to offer advice.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:19.350
I was wondering what I'll
be doing 15 years from now.

00:15:20.130 --> 00:15:21.730
15 years from now?

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:24.760
That's an unusual thing
to be worried about.

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:30.980
Remember when I was little, I used
to say a lot that I saw ghosts?

00:15:30.980 --> 00:15:33.490
Well, it seems that I was
actually seeing another world.

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:35.700
Another world?

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:38.880
I'm told it's another dimension.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:52.430
Flying bomber!

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:56.640
Ow...

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.630
What are you doing,
you moron brother?!

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:02.480
How dare you call
your brother a moron?!

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:04.210
Right on!

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:06.210
I give up, I give up!

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:07.940
I'm tough!

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:11.360
Beating an elementary school kid is not
brag-worthy, you high school jerk!

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:14.290
You okay?

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:16.160
What do you mean?

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:19.000
You've been thinking a lot.
That's not like you.

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:21.460
Bro...

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:23.290
What's the matter, Isami?

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:27.230
Yuu says he's gonna take
the exams after all.

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:31.070
Oh, really? So you guys will be
attending different middle schools.

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:32.540
Yeah.

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:35.170
He's smart, so he's
bound to get accepted.

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:37.310
Yeah...

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:38.810
You lonely?

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:40.110
Yeah.

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:41.480
But you know what?

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:44.150
If you guys are truly friends...

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:47.050
your friendship won't change
no matter how far apart you are!

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:48.270
You're spitting all over the place!

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:51.330
Why, you! I'm going out of my way
to make you feel better!

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:53.090
Ow! Let go, you perverted freak!

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:54.320
This is impossible!

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.620
It's almost Obon time.

00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:59.490
Hey, that's right...

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:04.770
We'll have to get ready to
visit mom and dad's graves.

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:08.540
Yeah. Fumiko said she's
gonna make paper dolls again.

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:10.720
And you aren't?

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:14.970
I'm almost in middle school, y'know.
I got better things to do.

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:18.250
Oh, really? I guess
you're all grown-up now.

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:19.220
This is impossible...

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:23.360
We're goin' there to tell 'em that
their kids and grandma are all doing fine!

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:25.230
I know that, so let's go!

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:27.320
You little twerp...

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:34.300
Uchida-chan, shouldn't we have gone
somewhere a little more classy for our date?

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:36.320
It's cooler being in here than outside.

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:40.370
We've been ordered to be on
standby at home, but what's up?

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:42.610
I thought about it all last night.

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:43.450
And?

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:47.460
I'm now convinced that the Magic
Circle Project should be called off.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.380
Called off?

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:52.160
Doesn't Shinohara
call the shots in Ab-Com?

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:54.760
There's still a way.

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:56.930
I need to contact Professor Mayuzumi.

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:58.750
Uh... Mayuzumi?

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:03.200
Dr. Mayuzumi used to be
the Magic Circle Project leader...

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:05.130
but he resigned six months ago.

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:06.400
Resigned?

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:10.200
I believe that Dr. Mayuzumi
sensed the danger of this project.

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:14.280
That's why I want to see him
and be absolutely sure.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:17.660
So, do you know where this professor is?

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:21.310
Actually, we don't know of his
whereabouts after his resignation.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:24.700
I presume that he cut some
kind of a deal with Shinohara.

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:27.420
Will someone like that help us?

00:18:27.860 --> 00:18:30.890
Actually, I discovered
something interesting.

00:18:30.890 --> 00:18:32.320
And what's that?

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:37.000
Haruka-chan goes by her mother's
maiden name after the divorce of her parents.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:41.040
Don't tell me her old
last name is Mayuzumi?

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:42.430
You guessed it.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:45.740
He's her father?

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:49.640
Dr. Mayuzumi goes to visit
Haruka-chan every three months.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:53.900
If he has even an inkling
of this project's risk factor...

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:57.080
He's sure to come to his daughter.

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:05.260
Kosagi, I verified your behavioral data.

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:09.710
You disobeyed orders and attempted
to destroy the Dragon Torque.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:14.470
By policy, your actions
would merit severe punishment...

00:19:14.470 --> 00:19:15.800
but right now we don't
have that kind of time.

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:20.470
As soon as Fukuro takes action...

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:23.410
We must secure the
Dragon Torque this time.

00:19:24.210 --> 00:19:27.480
If we can eliminate Karasu,
securing it should be simple.

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:37.740
Really! What is Miho doing?!

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:40.390
She's always so late...

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:43.360
Don't mess with me, dammit.

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:47.200
She always takes forever to get ready
'cause she spends so much time primping.

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:03.780
Hey...

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:05.520
How are you doing, little girl?

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:07.420
Who are you, mister?

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:10.050
Oh, boy. "Mister," am I?

00:20:12.530 --> 00:20:14.190
Don't pick on Isami too much, you hear?

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:18.990
He's still just a kid.
Don't be so hard on him.

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:23.410
Actually, I guess he's still just a kid.

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:25.530
Who are you?

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:34.280
Mister?

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:36.540
He disappeared.

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:48.050
Karasu?

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:50.260
Huh?

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:52.810
Karasu?

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:58.900
Yuu!

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:05.370
You bookworm!

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:14.960
Are you gonna do everything
your momma says?!

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:18.800
Not true!

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:20.420
What's not true?!

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:22.930
I made the decision myself!

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:35.350
Thanks for worrying about me.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:38.310
Why would I worry?!

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:41.380
But I've made my decision.

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:45.250
Until now I just did everything
my mother told me to...

00:21:46.250 --> 00:21:48.080
...but this is the first decision
I've ever made for myself!

00:22:04.940 --> 00:22:06.430
Good luck with the exams.

00:22:08.240 --> 00:22:11.060
We're still friends,
no matter how far apart we are.

00:22:12.480 --> 00:22:13.560
Isami...

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:20.320
You haven't changed
since you were a kid...

00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:21.830
...Yuu.

00:22:22.120 --> 00:22:24.280
You haven't either... Isami.

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:27.320
I ran into Ai.

00:22:29.630 --> 00:22:32.900
Now I think I know why
you're drawn to this dimension.

00:22:33.670 --> 00:22:35.960
I will never regret it.

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:41.950
I will protect Haruka
for as long as I live.

00:22:47.180 --> 00:22:49.050
I guess it's inevitable.

00:22:50.470 --> 00:22:52.220
Yeah.

00:22:52.690 --> 00:22:55.220
The next time we meet may be the last...

00:22:56.590 --> 00:22:57.730
...Karasu.

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:30.380
A sleepless night

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:34.270
The sound of the second hand

00:23:34.270 --> 00:23:41.200
The rumble of the
refrigerator in the air

00:23:42.100 --> 00:23:45.990
Just as the moon
through the blinds...

00:23:45.990 --> 00:23:49.900
Waxes and wanes, someday...

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:56.490
The pain will change to warmth

00:23:56.490 --> 00:24:01.710
Boat of time...

00:24:02.300 --> 00:24:06.960
No matter where it flows...

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:13.090
Most likely we'll meet again

00:24:13.090 --> 00:24:16.730
From scars come the
footsteps of dawn

00:24:16.730 --> 00:24:19.930
Rather than sighing,
they secretly...

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:26.040
come pouring down
on every new day

00:24:26.040 --> 00:24:30.580
No matter what sky it is

00:24:42.230 --> 00:24:44.720
I'm dreaming again.

00:24:45.230 --> 00:24:47.060
That summer day's dream.

00:24:47.540 --> 00:24:49.340
Do not get in our way.

00:24:54.760 --> 00:24:57.390
I can hear his screams.

00:24:59.430 --> 00:25:03.180
I will protect the Haruka of this dimension!

00:25:04.320 --> 00:25:06.220
Next episode: The Battle

00:25:07.720 --> 00:25:10.050
Can't you just stop now?
